  "title": "ToonFaces",
  "description": "This dataset contains EEG recordings from an experiment investigating how stylized, exaggerated facial images enhance event-related potential (ERP) features relevant to emotion detection. The study demonstrates that artificially modified human faces elicit a stronger N170 component compared to natural faces, informing the design of affective brain-computer interfaces (BCIs). Participant identifying information has been removed for anonymization.",
  "methods_description": "EEG signals were recorded while participants viewed images of stylized faces and standard faces. Event-related potentials (ERPs) were analyzed, with particular focus on the N170 component as a neural correlate of facial encoding and emotion processing.",
